From d63a94570837f3be6c73bb2469b9f5e47990615b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 21:52:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] DVDVideoCodecDRMPRIME: a Blu-ray picture before the IN time
 of its play item is decoded and not presented

With libbluray-9091 the primary video of a play item that is not joined
seamlessly comes from the random-access picture before its IN time, and the
demuxer marks the packets of the pictures presented before IN
(DemuxPacket::decodeOnly, 0bb686a). CDVDVideoCodecFFmpeg leaves their
pictures out after the pairing of the layers; the DRM PRIME decoder
(videoplayer.useprimedecoder) did not look at the mark, and showed them:
up to a second of pictures that the play item does not present, those of
another cut of a film with seamless branching among them.

It now gives FFmpeg the mark of the packet, AV_PKT_FLAG_DISCARD, which is
what it is for in libavcodec: decode.c puts AV_FRAME_FLAG_DISCARD on the
picture of such a packet (ff_decode_frame_props_from_pkt(), from
ff_get_buffer() before a hardware decoder allocates the frame, also with
frame threads) and drops it once it is decoded, in the simple decoding API
(MPEG-2, H.264, VC-1) and in the one of HEVC alike, unless the decoder asks
for AV_CODEC_FLAG2_SKIP_MANUAL, which this one does not. No layers are
paired in this decoder, so nothing has to see the picture first. The FFmpeg
decoder keeps its own mark, after the pairing.

Tests (outside the tree): discard_wiring.py, the calls in the tree (2 of its
checks fail before this change); t_discard.c, FFmpeg 9.0.2 from the image's
patched source built for the host, an MPEG-2 stream with reordered pictures
made by its own encoder, IN at a picture predicted from the random-access
one before it: with the mark, 57 of 60 pictures come out, those from IN on,
each the same to the byte as in a decode of the whole stream, with one
thread and with four; without it (the decoder before this change) the 3
pictures before IN come out too. The path of HEVC (receive_frame) was read
in decode.c, not run: no HEVC stream with reordered pictures is on the host.
---
 .../VideoPlayer/DVDCodecs/Video/DVDVideoCodecDRMPRIME.cpp | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDCodecs/Video/DVDVideoCodecDRMPRIME.cpp b/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDCodecs/Video/DVDVideoCodecDRMPRIME.cpp
index 91a427e..e1b4912 100644
--- a/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDCodecs/Video/DVDVideoCodecDRMPRIME.cpp
+++ b/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDCodecs/Video/DVDVideoCodecDRMPRIME.cpp
@@ -511,6 +511,14 @@ bool CDVDVideoCodecDRMPRIME::AddData(const DemuxPacket& packet)
                    : static_cast<int64_t>(packet.pts / DVD_TIME_BASE * AV_TIME_BASE);
   avpkt->side_data = static_cast<AVPacketSideData*>(packet.pSideData);
   avpkt->side_data_elems = packet.iSideDataElems;
+  // Hades: the picture of a packet that is decoded for the pictures after it and not presented (a
+  // Blu-ray picture before the IN time of its play item: DemuxPacket::decodeOnly) is left out by
+  // FFmpeg itself: AV_PKT_FLAG_DISCARD puts AV_FRAME_FLAG_DISCARD on its picture, which
+  // libavcodec/decode.c drops once it is decoded (with threads, and with a hardware decoder,
+  // alike; not with AV_CODEC_FLAG2_SKIP_MANUAL, which this decoder does not set). No layers are
+  // paired here, as CDVDVideoCodecFFmpeg pairs them before it leaves such a picture out.
+  if (packet.decodeOnly)
+    avpkt->flags |= AV_PKT_FLAG_DISCARD;
 
   int ret = avcodec_send_packet(m_pCodecContext, avpkt);
 
